## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a pragmatic CBA for on-device decision logic that changes user experience while preserving privacy and reducing server load. Tests modeling of energy, storage, and regulatory costs alongside rollout governance.

## Key Concepts

- On-device decisioning and privacy
- Compute and energy modeling
- Data minimization and consent logging
- Telemetry footprint and storage planning
- Rollout gates and break-even analysis

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo cost model for CBA
function cba(params) {
  const energy = params.cpuW * params.hours;
  const storage = params.rulesKB * params.devices / 1024;
  const savings = params.backendCostPerUnit * params.throughputReduction;
  const compliance = params.complianceCost;
  return energy + storage - savings + compliance;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate energy estimates across device SKUs?
- How would you adapt the model for regional regulatory differences?

## Why This Is Asked
Assess the candidate’s ability to structure a practical CBA for a distributed architecture shift, weighing latency, privacy, and cost against risk reduction and retention gains.

## Key Concepts
- Edge computing vs centralized analytics
- Inference costs, device storage, data transfer
- Regulatory/compliance penalties and risk
- Uplift in fraud detection and user retention
- Break-even analysis and sensitivity testing

## Code Example
```javascript
function breakEven(initialCost, monthlySavings, monthlyCosts) {
  let months = 0;
  let net = -initialCost;
  while (net < 0) {
    net += (monthlySavings - monthlyCosts);
    months++;
  }
  return months;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you design the data governance model to satisfy privacy regulations across regions?
- What mitigation plans exist if edge devices underperform (false positives, latency spikes, battery impact)?

## Why This Is Asked
This probes a candidate's ability to quantify costs for an on-device feature with privacy constraints and optional cloud lifts, focusing on edge-cases and governance.

## Key Concepts
- On-device storage budgeting
- Edge compute energy budget
- Privacy/compliance & consent overhead
- Rollout strategy and drift maintenance

## Code Example
```javascript
function estimateAnnualCost(storageMB, cpuW, users, cloudPerUser) {
  const storageCost = storageMB * 0.01;
  const energyCost = cpuW * 24 * 365 * 0.0003;
  const telemetry = users * cloudPerUser;
  return storageCost + energyCost + telemetry;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
